WEBVTT

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.720
Sangvis's massive artillery
and overwhelming numbers

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.600
put Griffin's secret base in grave danger.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.980
AR Team attacks the enemy's
base to stop the assault.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.900
Trust? It's been a long time
since I've heard that word.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.440
Oh, Commander Gentiane!

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.030
Welcome to Griffin's Top Secret base.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.740
This is M4A1!

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:36.740
Commander, come in!

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.870
Get down, everyone!

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.250
Stop their offensive and secure the base.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.460
Give me permission to
send all dolls outside

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.130
to find and destroy
the Sangvis base!

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:54.720
Do this your way then, rookie!

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.640
AR Team, I'm changing your priorities.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.010
Devote your full efforts to finding
and destroying the Sangvis base!

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.180
But Commander!

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:05.640
M4! I'm counting on you.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.270
Not this again.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:15.030
Quiet! Watch your surroundings!

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.360
No unusual signals.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.410
Clear.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.410
Look at the footsteps.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:23.410
The Ringleader here
probably just retreated.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.960
Three minutes ago, to be exact.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.960
I am the Sangvis Ferri T-Doll, Destroyer!

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.050
It's an honor to meet you.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.050
Is that the right thing to say?

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.390
On a long-range transmission, I mean.

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.140
I'm surprised, though!

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.890
You got here faster than I thought!

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.270
I was planning on taking advantage
of the chaos to make my next move!

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.110
But you even found my coordinates!

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.240
Griffin's not as useless as I thought!

00:01:55.240 --> 00:01:56.860
I'll give you credit for that.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.870
What was that for? I was still talking!

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.500
Nothing.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.540
Continue.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.960
Whatever.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.880
It's just one small base.
I don't care if I lose it.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.840
What are you planning?

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.640
Your little rust-bucket heads
could never figure it out!

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.270
You stupid Griffin dolls!

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.390
Just stay there and watch!

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.060
You can't do anything anyway.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.980
She left the channel.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.280
Can you follow?

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.610
She's not far.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:40.450
That moron didn't know
we were tracking her.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.870
She just left. We should
still be able to catch up.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.160
No, we should fall back.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.420
They're already monitoring our movements.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:53.790
If she calls reinforcements and
we're surrounded, we'll be finished.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:58.550
AR15, you're awfully calm this mission.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:03.300
I'm a realist. Always.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.640
Is something wrong with that?

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.310
Let's hurry. There's no time.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.580
It's the Commander!

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:56.670
Hooray! I'm back!

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:59.750
SOPII, you're bothering the commander!

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.260
Welcome back.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.840
Did the mission go well?

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:09.970
Yes. We destroyed their forward base
and are tracking their Ringleader.

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:12.970
All that's left is for you
to give the order.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.640
I see.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:15.850
Good work.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.400
You seem to have established a
good relationship with M4A1,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.650
Commander Gentiane.

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.860
Glad to see it's going well.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.030
But right now, I need to talk to you.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.160
AR Team will stand by at a
distance then, commander.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.910
No, it's fine.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.080
She's a special T-Doll.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:44.090
Take good care of her, and eventually
she'll reveal her true worth.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.930
Special dolls have a special
influence on those around them.

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:51.600
It's impossible to say
whether that influence

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.640
will bring us luck or disaster, though.

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:58.100
Our meeting here was top secret.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.520
As was the location of this base.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.650
The reason they were able
to launch a pinpoint attack

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.070
was probably that someone
told them about it.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.450
I will now make an important announcement.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.030
Our investigations showed

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:18.290
a doll generating serious errors when
transmitting and receiving data.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:21.540
It is an AR Team T-Doll,

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.960
AR15!

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:31.590
We discovered you were generating
serious errors during data upload.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.310
Thus, we will now shut down
your communication module

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.020
and take you to the interrogation
room for questioning.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.860
Raise your hands above
your head and come with us.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.320
That's impossible!

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.400
It must be a mistake!

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.570
Shut up, SOPII.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.570
This isn't your problem.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.040
No matter how much you whine,
we can't disobey orders.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.160
But...

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.540
AR15!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:04.670
Don't screw up the mission
just 'cause I'm not there.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.850
What are we looking at,
Commander Gentiane?

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.650
What happened?

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:31.240
So one of the dolls revealed
the base's location?

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.820
Of course not!

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:35.740
We wouldn't leak information!

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:44.250
Commander Shi Jun, if that doll's mind
was really taken over by the Sangvis,

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:47.750
we wouldn't be alive
right now to talk about it.

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.300
I know.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.220
I didn't really mean it.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:55.260
They definitely know
where the base is, though.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:59.220
The intel teams won't be
getting any sleep for a while.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:05.060
Commander, we made contact with the
Sangvis Ringleader when we hit the base.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:09.230
SOPII is sending you her signal.
It should be useful.

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:10.990
That's right!

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:12.490
Well done!

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:15.780
Give Helian the information.
And the top brass, too.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:19.040
They should be able to analyze
the Sangvis' movements.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.000
There'll be another mission, I think.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.910
So rest while you can.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.120
Okay!

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:31.510
She's just under suspicion right now.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:33.760
It's not a sure thing yet.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.680
There's no point in worrying.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.010
And we have a job to do right now.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:43.520
AR15 wouldn't want us
worrying about her forever.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:47.900
Why did it turn out this way?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.950
We've discovered the identity
of the Sangvis Ringleader

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.790
that attacked this base, everyone.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.580
Her name is Destroyer.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:07.290
She's a new type that has
long-range artillery capability.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:11.840
Command has designated
her a high-priority target.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:17.090
Commander Franklin,
share with them what we know.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:19.890
You're alive?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:23.480
You weren't here when the
Sangvis attacked, were you?

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:26.310
I thought you were dead.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:28.230
Coward.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:31.230
Who do you think made that resin you used?

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:35.110
I'm an engineer!
I don't fight on the front lines!

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.450
Anyway, look at the map.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:46.000
This is the Sangvis base
AR Team took out an hour ago.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:51.130
Our tracking data says that
Destroyer should still be in the area.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.880
That's a lot of ground to cover.

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.010
Yes.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.300
So we'll take another
step to narrow it down.

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:05.230
We'll send the dolls here to gather
Sangvis comms signatures.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.650
That will tell us the
Ringleader's precise location.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.020
High-altitude drones can't do it?

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:13.650
The Sangvis in this
area are well-defended.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.990
They shot down all the drones we sent up.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:25.040
Can we pull up the
geographic data for the zone?

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.290
We can.

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:32.880
Take out any areas with an
incline of 70 degrees or more.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.920
Okay.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.510
That's 60 percent.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:43.850
Now, then... this place
can be our Luxembourg.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:07.410
Sangvis planted an intrusion program
in AR15 before she returned to base.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:14.590
Her Zener Protocol's been cut, so she
can't exchange data with the outside.

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:20.680
We're also checking her feature code
and attempting a thorough virus removal.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:24.140
Given her value, we're not
going to be disarming her.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:29.140
But we need to find out where the virus
came from and stop it from coming back.

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:35.270
Anyway, until she comes back,
don't worry and focus on your mission.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:45.740
This mission is an extremely dangerous
one. Take backups of your minds, everyone.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:46.950
Right!

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.630
Hey, Dreamer!

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.840
How long am I supposed to stay here?

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:02.180
Hmm... I recommend
staying until nightfall.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:05.510
Your dumb ass would stand
out so much during the day,

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:08.770
that an average doll off
the street could find you.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:11.520
I'm ready to fight...

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.770
And don't call me a dumbass!

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:18.190
The only survivors you have
are our standard defense lines.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:23.990
You used up all the
extra forces I gave you.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:28.790
If I hadn't ordered you to move,
you'd be full of bullets right now.

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:34.960
Those useless Griffin
dolls couldn't hurt me.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.790
You'll know if that's true real soon.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.500
What?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.800
Griffin's coming from the northeast.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:44.180
What?!

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:49.310
This is Javelin Team!

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:52.230
We've wiped out a Sangvis patrol!

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.190
We're gathering comms signatures now!

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:56.400
Well done!

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:58.690
There are multiple pieces
of useful data here!

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:01.400
I'll send the codes to be
cross-validated immediately!

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.450
Get me more data!

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.240
Javelin Team, forward!

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.570
Right!

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:09.700
This is Harpoon Team.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.490
Sangvis has appeared to our front.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.500
We have engaged the enemy.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.580
Longsword has entered combat.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.420
We're encountering more enemies.

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:22.590
The Ringleader on their side
is getting ready for a fight.

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.300
There's nowhere for her to run.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.720
She'll show up sooner or later.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:32.770
We just need the chicken to watch
and make sure she doesn't get away.

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:35.350
I'm watching! I'm watching!

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:38.690
And I'm not a chicken!

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.110
Don't worry.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:44.070
Even if Franklin misses her,
we'll catch her.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.360
Fishing Net, you link up?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:49.280
Unit 794 will be there soon.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:54.120
Yes. We've already
reached the target point.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:56.290
We're waiting for their arrival

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:58.250
Cheer up, SOPII.

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.960
You're a doll, right?

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:05.590
If I'm a doll, that means I shouldn't
feel affected. So why do I?

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:08.930
We're just tools to send on missions.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:12.720
Why were we given pseudo-emotion modules?

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:17.270
Our only job is to aim for the
enemy's head and pull the trigger.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:25.490
Maybe the person who created us wanted
us to do more than just pull the trigger.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.700
SOPII, you okay?

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:31.280
I don't know.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.370
We were finally all together again.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.460
They're here, everyone.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.880
Y-You're...

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:48.550
<i>Gutentag.</i>

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:51.510
The 794 support unit has arrived.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:55.180
G43...

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:59.850
I thought AR team had four members.

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:01.600
Where's the other one?

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.770
Um, well...

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:08.990
Let's carry out the mission first.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:13.280
Right now, the other units are
attacking from all directions.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:17.160
If the Ringleader's going to run,
she'll likely use this route.

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:19.620
I see!

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.540
Then we'll provide fire support.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:29.050
Being sentimental won't change a thing.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:38.770
Nothing in the database
matches this signal pattern.

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:43.060
This is as deep inside her
neural cloud as we can go.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:47.480
We'll need 16LAB's
permission to go deeper.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:50.070
Fine. We'll call it a day.

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:54.280
Cut her Zener Protocol and send
her back to the interrogation room.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:03.170
Longsword has finished combat.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:07.130
Javelin has cleared its area of enemies!

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:10.550
Roger. Fishing Net, advancing!

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.180
Okay, keep up the pace!

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:15.220
All units, swap out and advance!

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.390
Hey, Dreamer!

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:24.400
Griffin's dolls are getting closer!

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.770
Do something!

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.480
She's not there?

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.610
Shit! Not now!

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:35.950
I lost all my Jaegers.

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.540
And I only have a few Rippers left.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:43.790
I can't take this anymore!

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:45.330
I'm leaving!

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.340
A strong Sangvis signal!

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:51.420
It's her!

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:54.800
Just like the commander said,
she came out when it got dark!

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.760
Vector M33X7.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.060
She's hiding near the river.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:01.020
Prepare the flares.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.230
Roger!

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:11.280
Griffin dolls? What are you doing here?

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.490
Your little rust-bucket head
could never figure it out!

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.280
You stupid Sangvis doll!

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.330
You're fighting one doll
with these numbers?

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:21.870
You should be ashamed!

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:25.500
Scatter!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:26.960
Watch for her shells!

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.510
Go to hell!

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:44.140
Emergency transmission to
all Griffin dolls and teams.

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:47.270
AR Team's T-Doll, AR15,

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:49.900
escaped the interrogation
room five minutes ago.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:57.320
This T-Doll may be infected with a Sangvis
virus, and is extremely dangerous.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:18:01.030
What's wrong?
Why are you just standing there?

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:07.040
Also, her Zener Protocol has been
turned off, so she can't be tracked.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.880
What are you doing?

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:12.130
Watch out!

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.350
You okay?

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:25.230
Report to command if you find her,

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:27.230
and apprehend her immediately.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:31.150
If needed, you are permitted
to attack or destroy her.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:36.780
You really are stupid if you're
spacing out in the middle of a fight!

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:38.950
You maggot!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.040
Now. Escape.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.330
Dreamer?

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.580
Damn it!

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:53.420
Where's Destroyer?

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:56.510
She escaped the encirclement!

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:57.760
No...

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:00.260
What was that?

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.590
I don't know.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:06.220
But that attack cut off our
communications with the outside!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:10.310
Why? And at a time like this...

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:13.940
You lost your command system, too?

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.780
Is it a coincidence...

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:19.860
...that it happened right when that
doll tried to make a run for it?

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:23.660
M4, what do we do now?

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:26.910
I want to go looking for AR15.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:28.750
But we're in the middle of a mission.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:33.960
Destroyer got away, but there
are still lots of Sangvis.

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:37.920
Which means we should
start by following Destroyer.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.180
What good would that do at this point?

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:41.930
Calm down, M4.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:46.640
Do you really think AR15
is being controlled?

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:51.350
If she fled of her own will, instead of
being controlled by Sangvis,

00:19:51.350 --> 00:19:53.810
she must have had something she had to do.

00:19:55.070 --> 00:20:00.900
You mean AR15 realized
Sangvis's deeper objective?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:06.990
But... But if she really did find
something, why didn't she report it?

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:09.660
Or even tell us?

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:14.040
M4, I know more about AR15 than you do.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:18.840
Or should I say I know more about AR Team?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:22.760
If that was her decision,
then there must be a reason.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:26.470
All we can do is believe in her.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:30.020
And for that, we have
to carry out our mission.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:34.440
M16 is right!

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.860
But we can't contact our
commander right now.

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:40.240
With no one to command us...

00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:43.610
I lost the memories of when
we fought together last,

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:48.030
but M4, you know what we can do.

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:52.660
We can handle the Sangvis
here by ourselves.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:55.290
Go, AR Team.

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:59.920
Your comrade believes
in you, too. I know it.

00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:06.970
Thank you, G43.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:11.810
You're right. She's a
treasured companion to us.

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:18.360
AR Team, let's follow Destroyer!

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:22.110
Dreamer...! Dreamer!

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:23.650
Hey... Dreamer!

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:26.950
What? What's wrong?

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:30.950
Griffin was way faster than we thought!

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:33.660
Use your firepower to slow them down!

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:37.170
Huh? Why do I need to do that?

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:43.300
You promised that when the mission
was complete, you'd support my retreat!

00:21:44.970 --> 00:21:48.390
So, is the mission complete?

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.970
I failed to assassinate Kryuger.

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:58.690
But the program I loaded
into AR15 worked fine!

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:04.110
I found the data on Safehouse 3
inside her neural cloud, too!

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:07.740
We have the data we need
for Parapluie now!

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:09.320
So help me!

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:17.370
If the mission's complete, there's no
need for you anymore, right?

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:22.300
We're dolls.

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:26.840
And dolls are expendable, right?

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:32.600
There's no reason to waste resources going
to pick up a piece of garbage, right?

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:37.520
Do you really think you
can get away with this?

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:41.360
You can revive as soon
as you're killed, anyway.

00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:45.940
You'll lose your memories of
what's happening now, too.

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:47.950
And when that happens,

00:22:47.950 --> 00:22:52.080
you'll be like a little puppy that
does whatever I tell her to!

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:54.410
That's... not true!

00:22:54.410 --> 00:22:56.200
You're lying!

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:57.750
You think so?

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:00.330
My adorable little moron...

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:04.340
You don't think this is
the first time, do you?

00:24:42.980 --> 00:24:46.360
Episode 10: "The Kindling 03."
